  "worked_solution": "Taking the square root of both sides of the inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & <10 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & <\\sqrt{10} \\\\ |x| & <\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the definition of absolute value, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt{10}<x<\\sqrt{10}.\n$$\n\nTherefore the solution is $x\\in (-\\sqrt{10},\\sqrt{10}).$",
